  <!-- 1. PAT -->
  <section id="pat">
    <div class="kicker">THE BASICS</div>
    <h2>🪙 What PAT is</h2>
    <p class="lead">PAT (Public Access Token) is the points currency of PATV. It's one balance shared by the website, the
      Camfrog rooms and Discord, so PAT you win from Pepe in a room is the same PAT you spend on the site.
      It isn't crypto and it isn't real money, but you can spend it on real prizes in the <a href="/shop">shop</a>.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>💬 Hang out</h3>
        <p>Chatting in a room enters you in Pepe's automatic raffles, and whoever spends the most time on mic each hour
          gets a top-mic reward. Chat messages and mic time also earn XP.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!xp</code> · <code>!level</code></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>⬆️ Level up</h3>
        <p>1 XP per chat message, 1 XP per second on mic. Every new level pays <strong>25,000 PAT</strong>, and every
          5th level is a <strong>milestone</strong>: a bonus of 250,000 PAT &times; (level &divide; 5) &mdash; 250k at
          level 5, 500k at 10, 1.25M at 25, 2.5M at 50 &mdash; plus a level cosmetic for your profile or
          <a href="/cosmetics">GTF avatar</a> (prestige borders every 10 levels past 50). You also get a stat point every
          10 levels for your heist character. Paid by the Federal Reserve: a milestone it can't cover yet is paid as
          soon as it can.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏅 Achievements</h3>
        <p>100 achievements for chatting, mic time, games, heists and more. Each one is a pixel badge on your profile,
          plus XP and a PAT bonus.</p>
        <div class="cmd"><code>!achievements</code> · <a href="/achievements">/achievements</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎲 Play</h3>
        <p>Spin the wheel, win at the tables, win trivia, crack a vault, collect on a good bet. Getting tipped counts too:
          anyone can send you PAT with <code>!tip</code>.</p>
        <div class="cmd">Broke? <code>!beg</code> for a small handout (only when you're nearly out).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card wide">
        <h3>👛 Your wallet and history</h3>
        <p>Your balance shows on your profile. <a href="/history">/history</a> lists every PAT transaction on your account
          (tips, wins, bets, bonuses), and <code>!history</code> shows your last five in chat.
          The <a href="/rankings">leaderboard</a> shows the top balances and the <b>total PAT supply</b>: every PAT that
          exists, in wallets, vaults, escrow and stashes. Link your Camfrog name on your profile (then type
          <code>!verify</code> with the code) so your room PAT and site PAT are one balance.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Flow -->
  <section id="flow">
    <div class="kicker">MONEY FLOW</div>
    <h2>🏛️ Where PAT goes</h2>
    <p class="lead">When you pay for something (a spin, a ticket, a fee, a paid command) that PAT doesn't vanish.
      <b>Spending never burns PAT.</b> It moves into one of the pools below, and those pools pay it back out as prizes,
      heist loot and rewards. (The one exception is the <a href="#burned">weekly surplus burn</a>.)</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏛️ The Federal Reserve</h3>
        <p>The central bank, in charge of monetary policy. It collects fines, purchases and fees nobody else funded,
          pays level-up and achievement rewards and raffles, insures the Bank against bad loans, and is the target of
          the legendary bank heist. <code>!reserve</code> shows its balance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎰 The House (casino jackpot)</h3>
        <p>The casino's bankroll. Wheel spins, rake, losing bets, the bingo cut and 60% of every lotto ticket go in;
          it pays the wheel, blackjack wins and the fixed lotto prizes. 15% of its profit refills the Casino vault that heists rob.
          <code>!jackpot</code> (or <code>!vault</code>) shows what's in it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎟️ The Lotto pot</h3>
        <p>A separate rolling jackpot fed by 40% of every lotto ticket. Only a lotto jackpot win is paid from it,
          so a big lotto winner never drains the House. Capped at 100M.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏦 The Bank &amp; 📈 Market maker</h3>
        <p>Two working vaults: the Bank lends PAT to players through Reserve loans, and the Market maker puts up the
          starting money for every prediction market. Together with the House they're the <a href="#protocol">capital vaults</a>
          you can stake in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🧭 The routing table</h3>
        <p>Every fee in the game has a row in one table that says where it goes. A fee goes to whoever funded the activity
          (market fees to the Market maker, loan interest to the Bank, casino margins to the House); fees with nothing
          behind them go to the Reserve, the jackpot or a gang's turf business. The admins tune the splits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🔒 Escrow</h3>
        <p>When you stake PAT on something that takes days (a wager, a market, a loan, a bounty, a bingo card) it leaves
          your wallet straight away and is held in escrow. Every step is recorded, so if Pepe restarts mid-game your
          PAT is either paid out or refunded: never lost, never paid twice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>You spend PAT</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Reserve · House · Lotto pot · Bank · Market maker · Turf</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Prizes · Loot · Rewards · Staker profits</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>Your wallet</span>
    </div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2a. Burned (1.99dk) -->
  <section id="burned">
    <div class="kicker">OUT OF CIRCULATION</div>
    <h2>🔥 Burned</h2>
    <p class="lead">Once a week the protocol settles its surplus. Rewards and pools are funded first, then a ~4-week incentive
      buffer and the Federal Reserve's 25M target. <b>Only what's left after all of that</b> moves to the burn reserve and is
      destroyed, so the total supply goes down. No wallet, vault or other pool is ever burned. Every burn is listed here.
      <span class="cfg">The weekly settlement is still being built; until it runs, the burn reserve stays empty.</span></p>
    <div class="grid" id="burnStats" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="card"><h3>🔥 Total burned</h3><p class="n" data-b="total">…</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Last 7 days</h3><p class="n" data-b="d7">…</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Last 30 days</h3><p class="n" data-b="d30">…</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tbl"><table aria-label="Burn log">
      <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>PAT</th><th>From</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="burnLog"><tr><td colspan="4">Loading…</td></tr></tbody>
    </table></div>
    <div class="top"><a href="#top">↑ top</a></div>
  </section>
  <script src="/public/js/burns.js?v=1" defer></script>

  <!-- 2b. Protocol -->
  <section id="protocol">
    <div class="kicker">UNDER THE HOOD</div>
