    <h3 class="h3s">🏗️ Capital vaults: PAT that does a job</h3>
    <p class="lead">Three of those pools are <b>capital vaults</b>. Each one holds PAT that does a real job in the game and
      earns from that job. You can put your own PAT in alongside it (that's staking) and earn or lose with it.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🏦 Bank</h3>
        <p>Funds Federal Reserve loans (<code>!loan reserve</code>). Earns the interest and late penalties.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> borrowers who don't pay. A loan 30 days late is a default: the Federal Reserve pays the Bank
          back and takes over collecting it. That's like deposit insurance (up to a big monthly limit), so only defaults
          beyond that would ever hit stakers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🎰 House</h3>
        <p>This <i>is</i> the casino bankroll: the jackpot that pays out wins. Earns the house edge: losing blackjack bets,
          hold'em rake, wheel spins, the lotto's margin and the bingo house cut.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> big wins, like a wheel jackpot or a blackjack streak. Casino heists don't touch it: they rob the separate Casino vault,
          which the House refills with 15% of its profit. Still the most up-and-down vault.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>📈 Market maker</h3>
        <p>Puts up the starting money (the "seed") for every new prediction market, then takes that market's 2% trading fees
          and whatever's left when it settles.</p>
        <p><b>Risk:</b> a market can lose at most its seed.</p>
        <p>Its value counts each open market at what it expects back when it settles (the pot minus the winning
          shares, weighted by the market's own odds), not at the seed, so a one-sided market shows its coming loss
          straight away instead of at settlement.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>🤖 Auto <span class="new">DEFAULT</span></h3>
        <p>A fund that holds all three for you, inside admin limits: <b>at least 40% Bank</b>, <b>at most 35% House</b>,
          <b>at most 25% Market maker</b>. Every day it leans toward whichever vault has done best over the last 30 days
          for the risk it took.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note"><b>You only earn from what you fund.</b> The protocol's own PAT sits in each vault right next to
      stakers' PAT, so everyone (the protocol included) earns and loses in proportion to what they put in.</div>

